WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.050
Hi there, Steve Kaufmann here again,
and I'm back in Vancouver back in

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:08.250
front of my real bookshelf, not the
curtain that I use in Palm Springs.

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:14.010
And today I wanna talk about a question or
answer question that I get very often, and

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:17.520
that is, which language should I study?

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:21.240
You know, people say, you know,
I'm very interested in French, but

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.430
I also am interested in Chinese.

00:00:23.430 --> 00:00:27.660
And so which one should I study and
can I study two at the same time?

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:31.950
All kinds of questions around the
subject of what language to study.

00:00:32.369 --> 00:00:38.010
So my answer is, you know, in
some cases we have no choice.

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:41.820
So if you're going to work for
a German company in Germany,

00:00:42.089 --> 00:00:43.739
obviously you're gonna learn German.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:48.599
If, uh, future employers are
at demanding a certain level of

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:50.519
English, then you have no choice.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:56.120
So there are situations where we have no
choice, but typically people who ask the

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:58.860
question "which language should I study?"

00:00:59.849 --> 00:01:01.080
are not in that situation.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:05.310
They are people who are learning
languages out of interest.

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:10.560
And since motivation is such a
big factor in language learning

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:16.390
success, the obvious answer is which
language are you keenest to learn?

00:01:16.445 --> 00:01:19.920
Where where are you most enthusiastic?

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:24.960
And the motivation to learn a
language can be, you know, anything.

00:01:25.839 --> 00:01:31.800
I've often said that it's, it's a pity
that in Canada, in the school system, kids

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:37.920
in the English language school system are
forced to learn French because that is one

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:40.320
of the two official languages of Canada.

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:43.110
That's not a very strong motivator.

00:01:43.949 --> 00:01:49.050
To some extent, I believe it doesn't
matter what you study, because

00:01:49.054 --> 00:01:54.075
once you get going, once you start
learning language and you know how

00:01:54.075 --> 00:01:57.945
to learn languages and you've done
it once and you've been successful.

00:01:58.215 --> 00:02:03.435
You can learn as many languages as
you want and uh, as you have time for.

00:02:03.735 --> 00:02:08.745
And so if kids in our, just to digress,
in our English language school system

00:02:08.745 --> 00:02:12.855
in Canada, were allowed to choose
the language they wanted to learn,

00:02:13.335 --> 00:02:17.955
they're more likely to succeed and
therefore enjoy language learning and

00:02:17.955 --> 00:02:19.835
therefore go on to learn other language.

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:24.299
By forcing them to learn French,
because it's the official language,

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:29.040
you end up discouraging a lot of people
who are forced to learn a language.

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:30.779
They're not very motivated to learn.

00:02:31.799 --> 00:02:35.310
Now, insofar as you know,
motivation to learn a language,

00:02:36.119 --> 00:02:37.260
it can be many different things.

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:41.549
If you see, if you look at the bookshelf
behind me and in particular the two

00:02:41.549 --> 00:02:44.679
skinny bookshelves that are full of CDs.

00:02:45.585 --> 00:02:49.695
We don't need CDs any longer because
we can download audio from the internet

00:02:49.695 --> 00:02:57.495
but I have material there in Czech, in
uh, Japanese, in French, in German, in

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:02.115
Swedish, um, Russian, uh, you name it.

00:03:02.115 --> 00:03:04.095
And similarly books, Latin even.

00:03:04.095 --> 00:03:05.025
I have books in latin.

00:03:05.025 --> 00:03:08.445
So any number of things
can trigger your interest.

00:03:09.495 --> 00:03:12.285
Right now, for example,
I'm focusing on Polish.

00:03:12.285 --> 00:03:16.065
I did some Danish because I'm gonna
be in Denmark and then in Poland.

00:03:16.424 --> 00:03:19.275
So a trip to the country
can be a motivator.

00:03:19.545 --> 00:03:22.665
So obviously if you're about to go
to a country, you're very, or if

00:03:22.665 --> 00:03:25.605
you know you're gonna go there in
six months, that's a big motivator.

00:03:26.144 --> 00:03:30.584
It could be a person, you know,
I found, uh, some of the CDs in

00:03:30.584 --> 00:03:33.795
themselves motivating because they
were so interesting to listen to.

00:03:34.305 --> 00:03:38.214
So, uh, but I, I still say
in a way it doesn't matter.

00:03:38.695 --> 00:03:42.960
Any time you invest in learning
a language, it's with you

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:44.580
and you can always go back.

00:03:44.609 --> 00:03:50.370
I have taken various stabs at learning
Korean prior to going to Korea, or

00:03:50.579 --> 00:03:55.230
for whatever reason, or maybe I think
initially I was motivated to learn Korean

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:59.940
because it seemed to me that it would
be easy after Chinese and Japanese.

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:03.360
That turned out not to be
a very strong motivator.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:09.390
The idea that a language might be
easy may not be as strong a motivator

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:14.250
as I'm gonna go to the country, or
I have a friend, or I'm interested

00:04:14.250 --> 00:04:16.079
in anime in the case of Japanese.

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:20.969
So you have to make sure that
the motivation is deep enough.

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:25.230
So in my case with Korea and the fact
that it's similar to, not similar,

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:29.370
but the Japanese and Chinese help
me in learning Korean was in itself

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:31.240
not a strong enough motivation.

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:39.375
Uh, when I was in Korea recently, four
years ago and, uh, was speaking some

00:04:39.375 --> 00:04:41.565
Korean, then that kind of motivated me.

00:04:41.805 --> 00:04:45.645
But then when I went away and I didn't
go back to Korean or to Korea, then

00:04:45.645 --> 00:04:48.015
my motivation declined somewhat.

00:04:48.345 --> 00:04:53.505
So it's important to find sort of
a motivator that is gonna keep you

00:04:53.505 --> 00:04:58.095
motivated, and very often that's just
the enjoyment of the language itself,

00:04:58.395 --> 00:05:02.595
the enjoyment of discovering things in
the language, reading about the history

00:05:02.595 --> 00:05:03.855
of the country and so forth and so on.

00:05:04.155 --> 00:05:08.355
But I, I guess my conclusion
on all of this is that which

00:05:08.905 --> 00:05:09.975
language should you learn?

00:05:10.035 --> 00:05:11.775
It doesn't really matter.

00:05:12.375 --> 00:05:16.335
Uh, even if you're only motivated for
a short period of time and then you

00:05:16.335 --> 00:05:21.195
lead that language and study some other
language, none of that is lost because

00:05:21.195 --> 00:05:26.505
when you go back to that language, you
will very soon pick up where you left off.

00:05:27.475 --> 00:05:31.935
So I like having quite a few
sort of irons in the fire.

00:05:32.265 --> 00:05:36.075
Uh, I've left my Arabic, I mean,
my Arabic is pretty bad right now.

00:05:36.825 --> 00:05:41.925
I was a lot better even a year ago, but
then I've spent more time on Persian and

00:05:41.930 --> 00:05:46.425
I'm spending time on, you know, I was
spending time on Danish and now on Polish.

00:05:47.685 --> 00:05:48.135
All good.

00:05:48.405 --> 00:05:50.355
You know, you don't lose anything.

00:05:50.895 --> 00:05:53.705
And as for this question of,
should I study two languages

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:55.385
at the same time, or not?

00:05:55.845 --> 00:05:58.905
Again, it depends on your
motive, uh, motivation.

00:05:59.385 --> 00:06:02.475
Um, obviously if you stay with
one language, you're gonna

00:06:02.475 --> 00:06:04.125
learn that language faster.

00:06:04.425 --> 00:06:08.655
If you try to do two languages at the
same time, you will discover a little

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:12.915
bit about two languages, but you won't
progress as far in the one language.

00:06:13.275 --> 00:06:18.299
Although sometimes, if you feel that
you're not making progress in one language

00:06:18.304 --> 00:06:22.260
and then you go to a second language
and it's fresh and new for you, and so

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:25.770
you have a sense of achievement in that
language, then when you go back to the

00:06:25.770 --> 00:06:28.919
first one, uh, you're kind of refreshed.

00:06:29.429 --> 00:06:32.520
The batteries are charged up
and you quickly pick up where

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:35.280
you left off and drive forward.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:40.650
So I guess my conclusion is, you know,
if you are in a situation where you

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:47.455
have to learn a language, try to find
something motivating about the language

00:06:47.475 --> 00:06:49.095
because you're gonna have to learn it.

00:06:49.755 --> 00:06:53.595
On the other hand, if you are in a
position where you have the luxury

00:06:53.595 --> 00:06:58.035
of choosing which language to learn,
go with your mood at the moment.

00:06:58.035 --> 00:07:01.875
If you're more motivated,
motivated to learn language a at a

00:07:01.875 --> 00:07:03.615
certain point in time, go for it.

00:07:04.185 --> 00:07:12.000
When the motivation for that language
seems to sag, go and do another language.

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:14.160
A language you're very motivated to learn.

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:16.170
You can always come back to the first one.

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:17.250
Nothing lost.

00:07:17.670 --> 00:07:21.270
Uh, tasting different languages
in different ways is always

00:07:21.270 --> 00:07:24.510
satisfying, always pleasurable.

00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:30.300
And uh, and the main thing is not to
worry about how well you're doing, uh,

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:32.140
if you don't have to learn the language.

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:34.650
You don't have to write an
exam if you're doing it out of.

00:07:35.565 --> 00:07:36.915
Don't compare yourself.

00:07:37.215 --> 00:07:39.165
Don't be too demanding of yourself.

00:07:39.345 --> 00:07:41.835
Just enjoy whatever you're
doing in the language.

00:07:42.285 --> 00:07:48.015
As Lomb Kato once said, uh, foreign
language is one thing that is

00:07:48.345 --> 00:07:52.425
worth learning, even imperfectly
or words to that effect...

00:07:52.485 --> 00:07:53.535
or learning poorly.

00:07:53.715 --> 00:07:57.875
So there is never a negative
to learning a language.

00:07:58.125 --> 00:08:00.775
So I would go with a mood of the moment.

00:08:01.115 --> 00:08:04.590
Which language am I most
motivated to learn right now?

00:08:04.619 --> 00:08:08.219
And that's my answer on which
language should I learn.

00:08:08.460 --> 00:08:09.840
I hope that was helpful.

